From 4e9b8c134414cbf5c70907247f9f557c0c57aa7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HiGarfield <HiGarfield@126.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 00:19:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/21] test: add one-command verification suite

Introduce tests/run.sh driving five phases:
  A  build gates (gcc/clang, -std=c89 -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic, -DTESTING,
     ASan/UBSan, optional libwrap) -- all must compile with zero warnings
  A2 cppcheck, phase B unit tests (one binary per tests/*.c),
  C  end-to-end daemon tests (tests/functional.py), D the same traffic
  under ASan/UBSan, E valgrind with leak and fd tracking.

tests/functional.py starts the real daemon against fake printer devices
(regular file, FIFO, and a pty for bidirectional mode) and verifies
byte-level integrity with sha256: 1 byte, the 8K ring-buffer wrap
boundaries, 1 MiB, slow chunked sends, half-close tail delivery, client
RST and mid-transfer disconnect, sequential and simultaneous connections,
bidirectional printer-to-network responses, IPv6, and survival when the
printer stalls or disappears.

The suite enforces ANSI C89, which surfaced one real violation:
test_write_eof_deadcode_removed.c declared its loop variable inside the
for-initialiser. Hoist it.

