Subject: [PATCH 07/21] feat(config): add a -t idle-timeout option

Upstream 0.97 has no -t at all; the idle timeout was the compile-time
IDLE_TIMEOUT_SEC only.  Add -t <seconds> so an operator can shorten or
lengthen the window without rebuilding, and 0 to disable it.

Parsing uses strtol() rather than atoi() so junk, empty strings, negative
values and overflow are rejected instead of silently becoming 0: '-t abc'
quietly meaning 'never time out' is exactly the failure mode worth
avoiding.  The message names the option so the mistake is obvious.

Deliberately NOT configurable: the post-EOF grace window that lets a
printer reply arriving just after the host finished sending still be
forwarded.  That window is what guarantees a job terminates, so exposing
'wait forever' here would let one silent printer pin a connection open.

Tests (tests/functional.py): -t 1 tears an idle job down (bounded below
3.5s so an ignored -t fails, mutation-verified at 5.33s), -t 0 keeps the
connection open, and abc/-1/overflow are refused with a clear message.

Resolves U7.
