Subject: [PATCH 13/21] test(portability): add 32-bit and musl build gates

A single 64-bit glibc build hides assumptions about word size and libc:
sizeof(long), the width of pid_t, and which headers a given libc exposes
transitively.  Add two gates that must also compile with zero warnings --
-m32 for a 32-bit target and musl-gcc for a second C library.

Both are probed before use, so a host without 32-bit multilib or without
musl SKIPs the gate instead of failing the suite.

Still out of reach here: arm/mips cross compilation.  The distro carries
gcc-arm-linux-gnueabi and gcc-mips-linux-gnu but installing them needs
root, which this environment does not have, so big-endian targets remain
unexercised and are recorded as such rather than claimed as verified.

Resolves U6 (partially: cross targets still need a CI runner).
