Subject: [PATCH 17/21] fix(security): refuse numeric -u/-g ids that do not fit
 (Fixes #BUG-010)

resolve_user()/resolve_group() accepted any numeric value that strtol()
could parse and cast it to uid_t/gid_t.  A value wider than those types
is truncated silently, and truncation to 0 means "root": an operator
asking to drop privileges with -u 4294967296 would have been told
"running as uid=0 gid=0" and kept full privileges, which is exactly the
outcome -u exists to prevent.

Both now verify the value survives a round trip through the target type
and reject it otherwise, so the failure is reported as an unknown
account instead of a silent no-op.

