Subject: [PATCH 18/21] fix(build): keep the caller's -W flags and set install
 modes (Fixes #BUG-011)

The Makefile rebuilt CFLAGS as $(filter-out -W%, $(CFLAGS)) -Wall -Wextra,
so every -W switch a caller supplied was thrown away.  Distribution build
flags routinely include hardening switches of exactly that shape --
Ubuntu's dpkg-buildflags adds -Werror=format-security -- and dropping
them meant the package build silently lost the check it asked for.

The project's own warnings are now appended to whatever the caller passed
instead of replacing it.  Install also sets the modes explicitly rather
than inheriting them from the working tree, so the binary and the init
script are always executable and the config and man page always 0644.

Gate (fails while the filter-out is in place):
  makefile-keeps-user-wflags in tests/run.sh
